{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/2/context.json","@type":"sc:Manifest","@id":"https://cdm21010.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/Handschriften:12155/manifest.json","label":"[Book of prayer] / (Hs 610)","metadata":[{"label":"Translation of Title","value":"Gebedenboek"},{"label":"Associated Body","value":"Maagdendries monastery, Maastricht, former owner"},{"label":"Country of Production","value":"Netherlands"},{"label":"Subject - Genre/Form","value":"manuscripts (documents) | illuminated manuscripts | prayer books | Manuscripts | Devotional literature | Prayers and devotions | Prayers | Prières | Medieval manuscript | Devotions | Devotional literature | Illuminated manuscript | Prayer book"},{"label":"Year of Creation","value":"1500"},{"label":"Associated Name","value":"Bonen, Catharina, former owner | \nDaele, Elisabeth van den, former owner | \nKeller, Alexander, former owner"},{"label":"Varying Form of Title","value":"Hier beginnen die ghetijden vander hoegher moeghender werdigher heiligher drivuldicheit"},{"label":"Provenance","value":"Maagdendries monastery, Maastricht: Catharina Bonen, Elisabeth van den Daele; Alexander Keller (ca. 1897). Purchase by Radboud University from an antiquarian bookseller in 2020. | \nTwo 16th-century owner&#x27;s inscription on the last free endpaper: &quot;desen bock hoert to suster catterena bonen&quot; and &quot;desen bock hooirt to suster elsabiet&quot;. Catharina Bonen was procuratrix in Maagdendries in 1490 and the years after. The second annotation may concern Elisabeth van den Daele, who was procuratrix in 1517 and 1519. | \nOn the same last free endpaper: &quot;Graf Alexander Keller 1897&quot;. | \nArmorial bookplate of the &quot;Comte de Keller&quot; (Gustav Ludwig Emil von Keller?) on the front paste-down with the motto &quot;Vaillant et veillant&quot; with underneath the text &quot;Stern / Paris&quot;. | \nInscription on the front paste-down in the same hand as the one by &quot;suster elsabiet&quot;: &quot;Ick wensse myn siel aen Godt Endt myn lichaem aen de erden&quot; . | \nPart of auction catalogue mounted on f. 1r, dated later than 1912, based on the contents."},{"label":"Place and Date of Origin","value":"Maastricht : tertiary monastery Maagdendries, ca. 1500"},{"label":"Language","value":"Dutch"},{"label":"General Note","value":"The Maagdendries monastery is also known as the St. Andrew&#x27;s monastery. | \nThe manuscript consists of 499 leaves, foliated 1-497. The leaf between f. 137 and f. 138 is not foliated. | \nHsLocalisation = The manuscript can be attributed to the Maagdendries monastery based upon the binding, the owner&#x27;s inscriptions and the contents (for more information: see Oosterman 2022). | \nHsColophon = Colophon on f. 203v: &quot;Bidt om gods wille enen ave maria voer die scrijfersse l v b&quot;. | \nHsScribe = The manuscript is written by a woman from the Maagdendries monastery, as the colophon mentions &quot;scrijfsersse&quot;. | \nHsBinding = Contemporary binding, brown calf over wooden boards, original fastenings (only one leather strap is changed), blind-tooled boards with the panel stamp of St. Servatius on both boards. The binding, including the used panel stamp, is almost identical to four other manuscript from the Maagdendries monastery. | \nHsDecoration = pen-flourished and ink-drawn initials, 6 (inserted) historiated initials. Contains 6 historiated initials, inserted from another manuscript, likely a choir book (music notation on the rear side of the initials) from the Cologne region: (f. 1v) David who felled Goliath; (f. 129r) David knocks off the head of Goliath; (f. 203r) David presenting the head of Goliath to two women; (f. 275r) King David on his throne. Four women make music and sing; (f. 352r) Coronation of the Virgin; (f. 430r) David watches as Bathsheba bathes. | \nHsLanguage = Dutch. | \nHsBibliography = Johan Oosterman, &#x27;Het gebedenboek van Catharina Bonen (Nijmegen, UB, Hs 610).  De rijke gebedscultuur in Limburgse vrouwenkloosters&#x27;, in: Publications de la Société Historique et Archéologique dans le Limbourg, à Maestricht 157 (2022), pp. 85-134. | \nHs 610 has been digitized by the mobile scanning team of eCodicesNL in 2021, with thanks to Sebastiaan van Daalen and Mariken Teeuwen."},{"label":"OCLC Number (OCN)","value":"1435844619"},{"label":"Physical Medium, Script and Lay-out","value":"paper and parchment, handwritten, littera hybrida (one hand), writing area: 24 lines on 99 x 64 mm"},{"label":"LHR Number","value":"362098431"},{"label":"Link to RUQuest","value":"https://ru.on.worldcat.org/oclc/1435844619"},{"label":"Physical Description","value":"1 volume (499 leaves) : pen-flourished and ink-drawn initials, 6 (inserted) historiated initials ; 145 x 103 mm"},{"label":"Shelf Mark","value":"Hs 610"},{"label":"Subject - Radboud Theme","value":"Religie en kloosterleven;"},{"label":"Subject - Chronological","value":"Middle Ages | Fifteenth century | Sixteenth century"},{"label":"Subject - Topic","value":"monasteries (institutions) | private devotion | Manuscripts, Medieval | Illumination of books and manuscripts, Medieval | Initials | Historiated initials | Prayer books | Penwork (Decoration) | Passion of Jesus Christ | Monastic libraries | historiated initial | Passion"},{"label":"Subject - Geographic Name","value":"Netherlands | Netherlands, Maastricht | Maastricht"},{"label":"Summary","value":"Prayer book made by and for the tertiary monastery Maagdendries in Maastricht, consisting of two different parts (based on the contents; not codicological), different in character. Such a consistent grouping is quite rare in prayer books. Part 1 contains prayers on the Passion and prayers for the Mass. Part 2 contains prayers on the Holy Virgin. The manuscript does not contain any prayers on saints or prayers for the church year. Therefore, the manuscript doesn&#x27;t contain a liturgical calendar, as it would not be functional. For an extensive description of the contents, including incipits, see Oosterman 2022."},{"label":"Title","value":"[Book of prayer] / (Hs 610)"},{"label":"Repository","value":"English Title"},{"label":"Source","value":"<span>From: <a href=\"https://bijzonderecollecties.ubn.ru.nl/digital/collection/Handschriften/id/12155\">[Book of prayer] / (Hs 610)</a></span>"}],"seeAlso":{"@id":"https://cdm21010.contentdm.oclc.org/oai/oai.php?verb=GetRecord&identifier=oai:cdm21010.contentdm.oclc.org:Handschriften/12155&metadataPrefix=oai_qdc","format":"application/xml","profile":"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/OAI-PMH.xsd"},"within":"https://cdm21010.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/Handschriften/manifest.json","sequences":[{"@id":"https://cdm21010.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/Handschriften:12155/sequence/s0","@type":"sc:Sequence","label":"[Book of prayer] / (Hs 610)","canvases":[{"@id":"https://cdm21010.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/Handschriften:11155/canvas/c0","@type":"sc:Canvas","label":"UBN_610_001r","images":[{"@id":"https://cdm21010.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/Handschriften:11155/annotation/a0","@type":"oa:Annotation","motivation":"sc:painting","resource":{"@id":"https://cdm21010.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/2/Handschriften:11155/full/full/0/default.jpg","@type":"dctypes:Image","service":{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json","@id":"https://cdm21010.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/2/Handschriften:11155","width":3524,"height":4980,"tiles":[{"width":3524,"scaleFactors":[1,2,4,8,16]}],"profile":"http://iiif.io/api/image/2/level1.json","protocol":"http://iiif.io/api/image"},"format":"image/jpeg","width":3524,"height":4980},"on":"https://cdm21010.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/Handschriften:11155/canvas/c0"}],"width":3524,"height":4980},{"@id":"https://cdm21010.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/Handschriften:11156/canvas/c1","@type":"sc:Canvas","label":"UBN_610_001v","images":[{"@id":"https://cdm21010.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/Handschriften:11156/annotation/a1","@type":"oa:Annotation","motivation":"sc:painting","resource":{"@id":"https://cdm21010.contentdm.oclc.org/iiif/2/